<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    FR-09 success glyph: a solid disc with a checkmark knocked out of it.

    COLOUR COMES FROM THE THEME, NOT FROM THIS FILE

    The fill references ?attr/ufmStatusSuccess, so the glyph resolves against
    whichever ThemeOverlay.UFM.Colorblind.<Type>.<Strength> is applied and picks
    up that type's successor colour with no call-site tinting. Inflated from a
    context without the overlay it resolves to the base default and simply looks
    like the rest of the app, which is the correct degradation.

    SHAPE CARRIES THE MEANING, COLOUR ONLY REINFORCES IT

    The three status glyphs are deliberately distinct in silhouette (disc+check,
    triangle+bang, disc+cross) so they remain tellable apart in greyscale and for
    a reader who cannot perceive the remapped colours at all. That is why the
    checkmark is KNOCKED OUT rather than drawn on top: a cut-out mark reads
    against any background, whereas an overlay would need its own contrasting
    colour and would fail on the surfaces where it matters most.

    The knockout uses fillType="evenOdd": a point inside both the disc and the
    checkmark subpath crosses an even number of edges and is left unpainted.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">

    <path
        android:fillColor="?attr/ufmStatusSuccess"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M12,2 A10,10 0 1,0 12,22 A10,10 0 1,0 12,2 Z M10.5,16.2 L6.8,12.5 L8.2,11.1 L10.5,13.4 L15.8,8.1 L17.2,9.5 Z" />
</vector>
